    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_5-1-programming-tool-installation-and-introduction" tabindex="-1">5.1 Programming Tool Installation and Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-programming-tool-installation-and-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1 Programming Tool Installation and Introduction&quot;">​</a></h1><p>[TOC]</p><h2 id="_5-1-1-arduino-ide-installation-and-usage" tabindex="-1">5.1.1 Arduino IDE Installation and Usage <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-1-arduino-ide-installation-and-usage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1.1 Arduino IDE Installation and Usage&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_5-1-1-1-arduino-ide-installation-and-interface-introduction" tabindex="-1">5.1.1.1 Arduino IDE Installation and Interface Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-1-1-arduino-ide-installation-and-interface-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1.1.1 Arduino IDE Installation and Interface Introduction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Arduino IDE is software specifically designed for Arduino microcontrollers and offers powerful functionality. Regardless of the version, the installation process remains the same. This section uses the Windows version of Arduino IDE 2.2.1 as an example for explanation.</p><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The installation method for the Mac version can be found in this section&#39;s table of contents.</strong></p></div><ol><li><p>Locate the <a href="./.html"><strong>Arduino IDE Installation Package</strong></a> in the same directory as this document, as shown below, and double-click to open it. To download the latest version of the software, visit the Arduino official website <a href="https://www.arduino.cc/en/software" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong><u>https://www.arduino.cc/en/software</u></strong></a>.</p><img loading="lazy" height="138" width="118" src="' + _imports_0 + '" style="width:0.98403in;height:1.15069in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>Click <strong>I agree</strong> to proceed with the installation.</p></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="885" width="1126" src="' + _imports_3 + '" style="width:5.31528in;height:3.8375in;" alt="企业微信截图_17032376944987" class="common_img"><ol start="3"><li>Select the default checked option and click <strong>Next</strong> to proceed to the next step.</li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="885" width="1126" src="' + _imports_4 + '" style="width:5.31528in;height:3.85833in;" alt="2" class="common_img"><ol start="4"><li>Click <strong>Browse...</strong> to select the installation path, and then click <strong>Install</strong> to start installation.</li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="885" width="1126" src="' + _imports_5 + '" style="width:5.31528in;height:3.83889in;" alt="3" class="common_img"><ol start="5"><li>Wait for the software installation to complete.</li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="388" width="499" src="' + _imports_6 + '" style="width:5.31528in;height:3.83125in;" alt="4" class="common_img"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>If the installation process prompts that a chip driver needs to be installed, check &quot;Always trust software from Arduino LLC (A)&quot;, and then click Install.</strong></p></div><ol start="6"><li>After installation is complete, click <strong>Finish</strong>.</li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="388" width="499" src="' + _imports_7 + '" style="width:5.31528in;height:3.80486in;" alt="5" class="common_img"><ul><li><strong>Interface Layout Overview</strong></li></ul><p>The main interface of the Arduino IDE is shown in the figure below and can be divided into five areas:</p><img loading="lazy" height="1047" width="1388" src="' + _imports_8 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:4.44792in;" alt="IMG_256" class="common_img"><ol><li><strong>Menu Bar</strong>: Responsible for settings related to the Arduino IDE.</li></ol><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th><strong>Icon</strong></th><th><strong>Function</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="22" width="30" src="' + _imports_9 + '" style="width:0.39375in;height:0.19167in;"></td><td>File options for creating or opening project files and setting interface preferences</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="20" width="31" src="' + _imports_10 + '" style="width:0.39375in;height:0.19167in;"></td><td>Edit options for code editing such as comments, indentation, and search</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="21" width="44" src="' + _imports_11 + '" style="width:0.39375in;height:0.19167in;"></td><td>Sketch options for configuring the entire project, including compiling and running, adding library files, etc.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="21" width="39" src="' + _imports_12 + '" style="width:0.39375in;height:0.19167in;"></td><td>Tool options for selecting the development board and port, and obtaining development board information, etc.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="20" width="32" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:0.51181in;height:0.17708in;"></td><td>Help options for getting started and resolving common issues, etc.</td></tr></tbody></table><ol start="2"><li><strong>Toolbar</strong>: provides tools related to the project, including the compiler, upload, serial monitor, and other tools.</li></ol><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th><strong>Icon</strong></th><th><strong>Function</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="38" width="41" src="' + _imports_24 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Verify: checks whether a program is written correctly, and compiles the project if no errors.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="38" width="40" src="' + _imports_25 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Upload: uploads the program to the Arduino controller.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="37" width="40" src="' + _imports_14 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Debug: some development boards support real-time debugging via Arduino IDE.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="41" width="242" src="' + _imports_17$1 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td>Select Board: allows different development boards to be selected for project development.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="36" width="33" src="' + _imports_16 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Serial Plotter: plots data printed to the Arduino serial port into charts.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="35" width="39" src="' + _imports_17 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Serial Monitor: prints serial port information.</td></tr></tbody></table><ol start="3"><li><p><strong>Editing Area</strong>: the area for editing code.</p></li><li><p><strong>Status Bar</strong>: displays the current editor status, such as the code line and column, development board information, etc.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sidebar</strong>: the core of the Arduino IDE, responsible for displaying the working folder, code debugging, library installation, and more.</p></li></ol><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th><strong>Icon</strong></th><th><strong>Function</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="46" width="44" src="' + _imports_18 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Sketchbook: displays the files of the current project.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="44" width="47" src="' + _imports_19 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Boards Manager: adds development board toolkits.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="45" width="43" src="' + _imports_20 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Library Manager: adds or removes program library files.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="44" width="41" src="' + _imports_21 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Debug: performs real-time debugging of the project.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="42" width="42" src="' + _imports_22 + '" style="width:50px;"></td><td>Search: searches or replaces code or variables.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_5-1-1-2-arduino-ide-usage-instructions" tabindex="-1">5.1.1.2 Arduino IDE Usage Instructions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-1-2-arduino-ide-usage-instructions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1.1.2 Arduino IDE Usage Instructions&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Arduino IDE Interface Settings</strong></li></ul><ol><li><p>Change the interface language: In the Arduino IDE interface, select <strong>File</strong> &gt; <strong>Preferences</strong>. In the pop-up window, select the desired language from the <strong>Language</strong> option, then click <strong>OK</strong>.</p><img loading="lazy" height="530" width="797" src="' + _imports_25$1 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:4.19653in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>By selecting <strong>File &gt; Preferences</strong>, settings such as the project file path, editor font size, and color theme can be modified in the pop-up window.</p><img loading="lazy" height="536" width="796" src="' + _imports_26$1 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.81319in;" class="common_img"></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Arduino Program Upload</strong></li></ul><ol><li><p>The example code that prints <strong>hiwonder</strong> is used here for illustration. Open the <strong>Demo.ino</strong> example program by double-clicking it in the <a href="./.html"><strong>Demo</strong></a> folder located in the same directory as this document.</p><img loading="lazy" height="1033" width="1906" src="' + _imports_27 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.37986in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>Connect the ESP32 controller to the computer via a data cable.</p><img loading="lazy" height="884" width="1268" src="' + _imports_26 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:4.01736in;" alt="开源6路舵机控制器接ESP32再连接电脑" class="common_img"></li><li><p>In the <strong>Select Board</strong> option, find the development board corresponding to Arduino. <strong>The COM port is not unique. The COM number can be checked in Device Manager. COM6 is used here as an example.</strong></p><img loading="lazy" height="659" width="1036" src="' + _imports_28$1 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.69028in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>Click the <img loading="lazy" height="38" width="41" src="' + _imports_28 + '" style="width:0.42708in;height:0.39583in;" class="inline-icon"> button to compile the program and verify whether the program has any syntax errors or other issues.</p><img loading="lazy" height="1033" width="1906" src="' + _imports_30$1 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.60972in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>After successful compilation, click the <strong><img loading="lazy" height="37" width="39" src="' + _imports_30 + '" style="width:0.40625in;height:0.38542in;" class="inline-icon"></strong> button to upload the program to the ESP32 controller.</p><img loading="lazy" height="1033" width="1906" src="' + _imports_32$1 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.60972in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>After the upload is complete, click <img loading="lazy" height="35" width="35" src="' + _imports_32 + '" style="width:0.36458in;height:0.36458in;" class="inline-icon"> to open the Serial Monitor, where the message <strong>hiwonder</strong> is printed.</p><img loading="lazy" height="1033" width="1906" src="' + _imports_34 + '" style="width:5.76389in;height:3.37986in;" class="common_img"></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Library File Import</strong></li></ul><p>To run the program, the required <strong>u8g2</strong> and <strong>LeArm_Kinematics_lib library</strong> files need to be imported. The procedure is described below, with the <strong>u8g2</strong> library used as an example to demonstrate the import steps.</p><ol><li><p>In the Arduino IDE, select <strong>Sketch &gt; Include Library &gt; Add .ZIP Library</strong>.</p><img loading="lazy" height="516" width="864" src="' + _imports_36$1 + '" style="width:5.76667in;height:3.81597in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>In the pop-up window, find <strong>u8g2.zip</strong> in the <a href="./.html"><strong>ArduinoIDE Installation Package</strong></a> folder, which is in the same directory as this document, and click Open.</p><img loading="lazy" height="31" width="493" src="' + _imports_35 + '" style="width:5.13542in;height:0.32292in;" class="common_img"></li><li><p>If the following prompt appears, the library file installation is complete.</p><img loading="lazy" height="44" width="502" src="' + _imports_36 + '" style="width:5.22917in;height:0.45833in;" class="common_img"></li></ol>', 34)
